---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";

const title = "How to Convert HEIC to JPG – Step-by-Step Guide";
const description =
	"Step-by-step guide: how to convert HEIC photos to JPG on Windows, Mac, iPhone, and Android using our free online batch converter.";
---

<Layout title={title} description={description}>
	<section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-14 sm:px-6">
		<p class="text-sm text-zinc-500">Guide</p>
		<h1 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight">
			How to convert HEIC to JPG
		</h1>
		<p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-300">
			Converting HEIC photos to JPG is quick and completely free with our
			browser-based tool. Here's how to do it on any device, in under a
			minute.
		</p>

		<h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold">Step 1 – Open the converter</h2>
		<p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-300">
			Go to the <a href="/" class="underline">home page</a>. No sign-up, no
			downloads, nothing to install.
		</p>

		<h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-semibold">Step 2 – Add your photos</h2>
		<p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-300">
			Drag and drop your HEIC or HEIF files onto the drop zone, or click to
			browse. You can select one photo or hundreds at once — there's no
			limit. To pick a whole folder, press <code>Ctrl+A</code> (Windows /
			Linux) or <code>Cmd+A</code> (Mac) inside the file picker.
		</p>

		<h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-semibold">Step 3 – Convert</h2>
		<p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-300">
			Click <strong>"Convert to JPG"</strong>. Each photo is processed
			instantly on your own device. A green indicator appears next to every
			converted file.
		</p>

		<h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-semibold">Step 4 – Download</h2>
		<p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-300">
			Download each JPG individually, or click{" "}
			<strong>"Download all as ZIP"</strong> to grab the entire batch in one
			archive — perfect for emptying your camera roll in bulk.
		</p>

		<h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold">Why convert HEIC to JPG?</h2>
		<ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-300">
			<li>JPG opens everywhere — Windows, Android, Mac, web forms, email.</li>
			<li>Most online upload forms reject HEIC files.</li>
			<li>Old photo editors and printers don't support HEIC.</li>
			<li>JPG is universally accepted by social media platforms.</li>
		</ul>

		<h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold">Frequently asked questions</h2>

		<h3 class="mt-6 font-medium">Does this work on iPhone and Android?</h3>
		<p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-300">
			Yes. The tool runs in any modern browser — Safari on iPhone, Chrome on
			Android — no app required.
		</p>

		<h3 class="mt-6 font-medium">Are my photos private?</h3>
		<p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-300">
			Completely. Conversion happens locally in your browser. Your photos are
			never uploaded to any server.
		</p>

		<h3 class="mt-6 font-medium">Can I convert thousands of photos?</h3>
		<p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-300">
			Yes. There's no file limit — the only constraint is your device's
			available memory.
		</p>

		<a
			href="/"
			class="mt-10 inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-lg bg-zinc-900 px-6 py-3 text-sm font-medium text-white transition hover:bg-zinc-700 dark:bg-white dark:text-zinc-900 dark:hover:bg-zinc-200"
		>
			Convert your HEIC photos now
		</a>
	</section>
</Layout>